# Every key below is consumed by GitHub Actions as a repo SECRET
# (`gh secret set <NAME>`), not read from a .env file at workflow runtime —
# GitHub Actions doesn't load .env files automatically. This file exists so
# every key this template needs is listed in one place, with what it's for
# and where it's actually consumed. Copy it to `.env` ONLY if you also need
# these values locally (testing workflows with `act`, running the app
# itself, calling the Slack webhook by hand to preview a message) — and
# never commit that `.env` (it's already in .gitignore).
#
# See docs/SETUP.md step 6 for the exact `gh secret set` commands.

# --- Required for the agent pipeline (agent-research.md, agent-dev.md, agent-review.md) ---
# One of these two. Runs Claude Code as the gh-aw workflow engine.
# Get an API key: https://console.anthropic.com/
# Get an OAuth token instead if you're on a Claude subscription plan rather
# than pay-as-you-go API billing: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/github-actions
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# --- Required for every Slack notification (ci.yml, deploy.yml, perf.yml, ---
# --- project-digest.yml, agent-notify.yml — see docs/WORKFLOWS.md)        ---
# Slack incoming webhook URL for the channel you want pipeline/agent
# notifications posted to. Create one: https://api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks
# Every workflow that posts to Slack checks this is set first and silently
# skips the notification if it's blank — so leaving this empty doesn't
# break anything, it just means no Slack messages.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Provided automatically by GitHub Actions — do NOT set this yourself ---
# GITHUB_TOKEN is injected by GitHub Actions into every workflow run
# automatically (github.token / secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN). It's listed here only
# so the full set of tokens this repo uses is visible in one place. You
# only need a personal value for this locally if you're testing `gh` CLI
# commands (project-digest.yml's stats gathering, gh-aw's safe-outputs) or
# workflows with `act` outside of Actions.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Your application's own env vars ---
# This template ships no application code (see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) — add
# whatever your actual stack needs below (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, a
# third-party API key, etc.) and set the production values as repo/
# environment secrets the same way as above, not by committing a real .env.
